@host = http://localhost:5187

# Story 07 - staff sign-in, refresh, sign-out, "who am I", and change password. Run top to bottom against a
# Development API (`docker compose up -d` first, then `dotnet run --project backend/src/Crm.Api --launch-profile http`).
# Seeded staff users (Crm.Modules.Identity.Contracts.DevSeed.IdentityDevSeed), password Identity:DevSeed:Password in
# appsettings.Development.json ("Crm_Dev_2026!"):
#   admin@crm.local        Administrator in all three departments
#   supervisor@crm.local   Supervisor in RYD-CARE, Agent in RYD-BILL
#   agent.a@crm.local      Agent in RYD-CARE
#   agent.b@crm.local      Agent in JED-CARE
# In Development the access token lives 2 minutes and a lockout lasts 2 minutes (appsettings.Development.json), so
# expiry and lockout can be walked by hand. Sign-in and refresh are limited to 30 per minute per IP in Development.
@ryCare = 06000000-0000-0000-0002-000000000001
@ryBill = 06000000-0000-0000-0002-000000000002

### 1. Login as admin - 200: accessToken, refreshToken, both expiries, tokenType "Bearer" and
### Set-Cookie: crm_refresh=...; path=/api/Agent/Auth; secure; samesite=strict; httponly.
### Paste the accessToken payload (2nd segment) into a base64url decoder: exp/iat/nbf are integers, `membership` is an
### array of "department|branch|role" strings (three for admin), `role` is ["Administrator"], plus sub/name/tenant_id/sid.
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. GET Me with no Authorization header - 401 urn:crm:problem:unauthorized (RFC 9457 body, not empty)
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Me

### 3. GET Me as admin - 200: displayName "System Administrator", preferredLocale "en", three memberships,
### roles ["Administrator"], all eight permissions
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 4. Login with the email upper-cased and padded - 200 (the email is normalised: trimmed, lower-case)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ADMIN@crm.local ", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

### 5. Login as supervisor - 200
# @name loginSupervisor
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "supervisor@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

@supervisorToken = {{loginSupervisor.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6. GET MyScope as supervisor - two departments (two `membership` claims arrived as several claims)
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/MyScope
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}

### 7a. Supervisor Me, no X-Crm-Scope - roles ["Agent","Supervisor"], permissions include tickets.assign
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Me
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}

### 7b. Supervisor Me with X-Crm-Scope: ryBill - roles ["Agent"], NO tickets.assign (effective permissions follow the
### active scope)
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Me
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}
X-Crm-Scope: {{ryBill}}

### 7c. Supervisor Me with X-Crm-Scope: ryCare - roles ["Supervisor"], has tickets.assign
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Me
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}
X-Crm-Scope: {{ryCare}}

### 8. Refresh (JSON body) - 200, a NEW refreshToken (the presented one is now rotated)
# @name refresh1
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{loginSupervisor.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### 9. Refresh again with the OLD token - 401 Identity.InvalidRefreshToken; the API log has the Warning
### "Refresh token reuse detected; session ... revoked"
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{loginSupervisor.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### 10. Refresh with the token from request 8 - 401 (reuse revoked the whole family)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh1.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### 11a. Login as agent A
# @name loginAgentA
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "agent.a@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

### 11b. Logout with its refresh token - 204 (the crm_refresh cookie is deleted too)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{loginAgentA.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### 11c. Refresh with it - 401 (logout revoked the session)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{loginAgentA.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### 12. Logout with a token that does not exist - 204 (idempotent, no oracle)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "not-a-token" }

### 13. Wrong password - 401 Identity.InvalidCredentials, detail "Invalid email or password."
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@crm.local", "password": "wrong-password-1" }

### 14. Unknown email - 401 with the SAME body as request 13 (never reveals whether the account exists)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody@crm.local", "password": "wrong-password-1" }

### 15a. Malformed email - 401, same body again
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "not-an-email", "password": "x" }

### 15b. Empty fields - 400 urn:crm:problem:validation (errors.Email, errors.Password)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "", "password": "" }

### 16. LOCKOUT - send this request FIVE times: five 401s; the fifth writes the Warning "account locked until ...".
### Then the CORRECT password (16b) is still 401 (locked). Wait Identity:Sessions:LockoutWindow (2 minutes in
### Development), then 16b - 200. Attempts while locked do not extend the lock.
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "agent.b@crm.local", "password": "wrong-password-1" }

### 16b. Correct password for agent B
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "agent.b@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

### 17a. Login as agent B (a second session; keep its tokens)
# @name loginAgentB2
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "agent.b@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

@agentBToken = {{loginAgentB2.response.body.accessToken}}

### 17b. Change password with a wrong current password - 400, errors.CurrentPassword
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Me/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentBToken}}

{ "currentPassword": "wrong", "newPassword": "Another_Pass_42" }

### 17c. New password equal to the current one - 400 (errors.NewPassword)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Me/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentBToken}}

{ "currentPassword": "Crm_Dev_2026!", "newPassword": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

### 17d. Too short - 400 (errors.NewPassword)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Me/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentBToken}}

{ "currentPassword": "Crm_Dev_2026!", "newPassword": "short" }

### 18a. Change agent B's password - 204. Every OTHER session of agent B is revoked (an older refresh token from
### request 16b now answers 401); THIS session's refresh token (request 17a) still answers 200.
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Me/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentBToken}}

{ "currentPassword": "Crm_Dev_2026!", "newPassword": "Another_Pass_42" }

### 18b. This session survives - refresh with the request 17a token - 200
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{loginAgentB2.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### 18c. Login with the new password - 200
# @name loginAgentB3
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "agent.b@crm.local", "password": "Another_Pass_42" }

### 18d. Change it back - 204
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Me/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAgentB3.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "currentPassword": "Another_Pass_42", "newPassword": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

### 19. ACCESS-TOKEN EXPIRY - re-send request 3 with an admin token more than two minutes old: 401 with
### WWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="invalid_token". Refresh (request 8 shape) - 200, then retry request 3 - 200.
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 20. RATE LIMIT - send request 13 repeatedly: past 30 attempts within a minute (Development) the answer is 429
### urn:crm:problem:rate-limited with a Retry-After header. Wait a minute before continuing.
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@crm.local", "password": "wrong-password-1" }
